@[syslinux page]
SYSLINUX (EXTLINUX for ext2/3/4, XFS and btrfs) boots BIOS machines only, not
UEFI. It isn't on this ISO: cast it with network (see @[todo boot-loader]).

Version 6.03 can't install to an ext4 filesystem with the "64bit" feature,
which mkfs.ext4 turns on by default. Check with
@[dumpe2fs -h /dev/sda2 | grep features]; if it lists 64bit, the filesystem
would have to be made again with @[mkfs.ext4 -O ^64bit] (or use GRUB).

In @[enchantment chroot], with /boot on the root partition /dev/sda2:
 @[mkdir -p /boot/syslinux]
 @[extlinux --install /boot/syslinux]
 @[dd bs=440 count=1 conv=notrunc if=/usr/share/syslinux/mbr.bin of=/dev/sda]
   (GPT disks: gptmbr.bin instead of mbr.bin)
 mark the root partition bootable, on MBR disks:
 @[sfdisk -A /dev/sda 2]
 or on GPT disks (the "legacy BIOS bootable" attribute):
 @[sfdisk --part-attrs /dev/sda 2 LegacyBIOSBootable]
Write /boot/syslinux/syslinux.cfg (your kernel version and root partition):
  DEFAULT smgl
  LABEL smgl
    LINUX /boot/vmlinuz-6.18.59
    APPEND root=/dev/sda2 rw
 @[exit]
After each new kernel, add it to syslinux.cfg.

